Supreme People's Court

Opinions on Further Deepening Judicial Openness

Fa Fa [2018] No. 20

Strengthening judicial openness is a major measure to implement the principles of the Constitution and laws and to ensure public participation in the judiciary. It is an important part of deepening the comprehensive supporting reforms of the judicial system and improving the operational mechanism of judicial power. It is an inevitable requirement for advancing the comprehensive rule of law and building a socialist country under the rule of law. Since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core has attached great importance to the work of judicial openness. The Third and Fourth Plenary Sessions of the 18th Central Committee regarded promoting judicial openness and building an open, dynamic, transparent, and convenient sunshine judicial mechanism as important tasks for comprehensively deepening reform and comprehensively governing the country according to law, and made a series of major deployments. The people's courts resolutely implemented the decisions and deployments of the Party Central Committee, closely focusing on the work goal of "striving to make the people feel fairness and justice in every judicial case," advancing judicial openness to an unprecedented breadth and depth, and achieving remarkable results. At present, the level of standardization, institutionalization, and informatization of judicial openness has been significantly improved. The four major platforms of openness of trial procedures, openness of court hearings, openness of judgments, and openness of enforcement information have been fully established and operated. An open, dynamic, transparent, and convenient sunshine judicial mechanism has been basically formed, playing an important role in safeguarding the people's rights to know, participate, express, and supervise; promoting the improvement of judicial service for the people and impartial justice; and promoting the spirit of the rule of law and telling the story of China's rule of law well. Judicial openness is a vivid practice of building a rule of law China in the new era, and has become a bright business card in China's international judicial exchanges and cooperation.

The 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China clearly put forward the major tasks of deepening the practice of governing the country according to law and deepening the comprehensive supporting reforms of the judicial system, and made new major deployments for deepening the openness of power operation, emphasizing that "the restriction and supervision of power operation should be strengthened, let the people supervise power, let power operate under the sun, and put power into the cage of the system," pointing out the direction for the people's courts to further deepen judicial openness and raising new and higher requirements. In order to deeply study and implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, implement a series of major decisions and deployments of the Party Central Committee on promoting judicial openness, summarize the experience of judicial openness work, consolidate the achievements made in judicial openness work since the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, promote the more mature and finalized open, dynamic, transparent, and convenient sunshine judicial mechanism, realize the modernization of the trial system and trial capacity, and promote new development of the work of the people's courts in the new era, the following opinions are put forward for further deepening judicial openness work.

1. General Requirements

1. Guiding ideology. Adhere to the guidance of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, fully implement the spirit of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and the First, Second, and Third Plenary Sessions of the 19th Central Committee, closely focus on the work goal of "striving to make the people feel fairness and justice in every judicial case," hold high the banner of reform and opening up in the new era, further deepen judicial openness, continuously expand the breadth and depth of judicial openness, improve and perfect the institutional mechanism system of judicial openness, optimize and upgrade the platforms and carriers of judicial openness, greatly enhance the refinement, standardization, and informatization level of judicial openness, promote the construction of a more open, dynamic, transparent, and convenient sunshine judicial mechanism, form a new pattern of comprehensively deepening judicial openness, promote the modernization of the trial system and trial capacity, vigorously promote the core socialist values, promote the enhancement of the rule of law consciousness of the whole people, tell the story of China's rule of law well, and spread the voice of China's rule of law.

2. Basic principles.

(1) Adhere to proactive openness. Deeply understand the important instructions and requirements of General Secretary Xi Jinping's "make no room for black-box operations, make judicial corruption nowhere to hide," fully recognize the great significance of deepening judicial openness work, further enhance the awareness of actively accepting supervision, truly change from passive openness to active openness, continue to improve and perfect the sunshine judicial mechanism, and strive to make justice not only achieved, but also achieved in a visible way.

(2) Adhere to openness according to law. Strictly fulfill the duty of open trial stipulated by the Constitution and laws, and effectively safeguard the people's right to participate in and supervise the judiciary. Strictly implement the scope of openness stipulated by law, and disclose relevant information according to law, while strictly observing state secrets and trial secrets, and protecting the information security of the parties. Respect the laws of the judiciary, clarify the content, scope, methods, and procedures of judicial openness, and ensure that judicial openness work is carried out in a standardized and orderly manner.

(3) Adhere to timely openness. Strictly follow the timeliness requirements of judicial openness, and any information within the scope of proactive openness shall be disclosed in a timely manner and not delayed without reason. For matters with clear deadlines for openness, the openness shall be strictly completed within the deadline. For matters without clear deadlines for openness, the openness shall be carried out within a reasonable time according to the nature and characteristics of the relevant information.

(4) Adhere to comprehensive openness. Take openness as the principle and non-disclosure as the exception, and promote judicial openness to cover all fields and all links of the work of the people's courts. Adhere to the combination of openness of procedural matters and openness of substantive content, the combination of openness of trial and enforcement information and openness of judicial administrative information, and the combination of openness through traditional methods and openness through new media methods, to maximize the protection of the people's rights to know, participate, express, and supervise.

(5) Adhere to substantive openness. Closely focus on the judicial needs of the people, promptly disclose according to law the judicial information that the parties and the public are most concerned about and most want to know, and effectively shift the focus of judicial openness to serving the needs of the masses and ensuring public participation. Continuously improve the interactive function, service function, and convenience function of the judicial openness platform, actively respond to social concerns, and strive to turn deepening judicial openness into a two-way interaction process between the people's courts and the masses, making judicial openness a bridge and bond for close contact with the masses.

2. Content and Scope of Further Deepening Judicial Openness

3. Comprehensively expand the scope of judicial openness. Respect the laws of judicial activities, and according to the functional positioning of courts at four levels, further clarify the content and scope of judicial openness. For judicial information involving the legitimate rights and interests of the parties, social public interests, and needing widespread public awareness, it shall be included in the scope of judicial openness, and according to its nature and characteristics, distinguish between disclosure to the parties or disclosure to the public. For information on the basic situation of the people's courts, trial and enforcement, litigation services, judicial reform, judicial administrative affairs, international judicial exchanges and cooperation, team building, etc., except for those that shall not be disclosed in accordance with laws, regulations, and judicial interpretations, or are otherwise not appropriate for disclosure, appropriate forms shall be adopted for proactive disclosure.

4. Deepen the disclosure of basic information of the people's courts. The people's courts shall proactively disclose the following basic information, adhere to dynamic updates, ensure accuracy, clarity, and easy access, and facilitate the people to obtain timely and accurate understanding.

(1) Institutional setup;

(2) Judicial interpretations;

(3) Guiding cases;

(4) Normative documents;

(5) Work reports submitted to the people's congress at the same level;

(6) Dynamic information such as important meetings, major events, and important work;

(7) Other basic information that needs widespread public awareness.

5. Deepen the disclosure of trial and enforcement information. The people's courts shall proactively disclose the following trial and enforcement information, gradually expand the scope of disclosure to cover all areas of trial and enforcement, improve and perfect the rules for disclosure of trial and enforcement information, promote the unification of disclosure process standards, and ensure that trial and enforcement power always operates under the sun.

(1) Judicial statistical information;

(2) Trial and enforcement process information;

(3) Court hearings of cases tried in open court;

(4) Judgments;

(5) Trial status of major cases;

(6) Enforcement work information;

(7) Information on commutation, parole, and temporary service of sentence outside prison;

(8) Information on enterprise bankruptcy and reorganization cases;

(9) Annual work status and typical cases in each trial and enforcement field;

(10) Research reports on judicial big data;

(11) Research results on trial and enforcement theory and judicial cases;

(12) Other trial and enforcement information involving the legitimate rights and interests of the parties, social public interests, or needing widespread public awareness.

6. Deepen the disclosure of litigation service information. The people's courts shall proactively disclose the following litigation service information, strive to enhance the convenience of obtaining litigation service information, improve the level of litigation services, and effectively facilitate the parties' litigation.

(1) Litigation guides;

(2) Announcements of the people's courts;

(3) Information related to judicial auctions and determination of reference prices for property disposal;

(4) Information on professional institutions and professionals such as judicial appraisal, evaluation, inspection, and audit; information on bankruptcy administrators; information on organizational diagnosis work for temporary service of sentence outside prison; information on expert databases;

(5) Information on specially invited mediators, specially invited mediation organizations, stationed duty lawyers, and expert volunteers participating in litigation services;

(6) Channels for petitioning and complaints;

(7) Other litigation service information involving the legitimate rights and interests of the parties, social public interests, or needing widespread public awareness.

7. Deepen the disclosure of judicial reform information. The people's courts shall proactively disclose the following judicial reform information, enhance the transparency of judicial reform work, and increase the people's sense of gain from judicial reform.

(1) Judicial reform documents of the people's courts;

(2) Progress of major judicial reform tasks of the people's courts;

(3) Typical cases of judicial reform of the people's courts;

(4) Other judicial reform information that needs widespread public awareness.

8. Deepen the disclosure of judicial administrative affairs information. The people's courts shall proactively disclose the following judicial administrative affairs information, promptly respond to social concerns, consciously accept social supervision, and effectively improve the transparency and standardization of handling judicial administrative affairs.

(1) Handling of suggestions and proposals of deputies to the National People's Congress and members of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference involving social public interests or social concerns;

(2) Budget and final account disclosure statements of departments;

(3) Informatization technical standards of the people's courts;

(4) Other judicial administrative affairs information that needs widespread public awareness.

9. Deepen the disclosure of international judicial exchanges and cooperation information. The people's courts shall proactively disclose the following international judicial exchanges and cooperation information, strengthen exchanges and mutual learning of judicial civilization, fully demonstrate the good international image of Chinese courts, and promote the enhancement of China's judicial international competitiveness, influence, and credibility.

(1) Important international judicial exchanges and cooperation activities carried out by the people's courts;

(2) Participation in important international judicial meetings by the people's courts;

(3) Other international judicial exchanges and cooperation information that needs widespread public awareness.

10. Deepen the disclosure of team building information. The people's courts shall proactively disclose the following team building information, facilitating the public to know, participate in, and supervise the team building work of the people's courts.

(1) Party building situation;

(2) Personnel work situation;

(3) Discipline inspection and supervision information;

(4) Information on advanced models;

(5) Education and training work situation;

(6) Judicial police work situation;

(7) Court culture construction situation;

(8) Other team building situations that need widespread public awareness.

11. Establish and improve the dynamic adjustment system for judicial openness content. According to the deployment and requirements of the Party Central Committee and the Supreme People's Court on judicial openness work, combined with public concerns and the actual situation of the people's courts, clarify the focus of judicial openness work on an annual basis, dynamically adjust and update the content of judicial openness, and steadily and orderly expand the scope of judicial openness.

12. Promote the standardization and normalization construction of judicial openness. The Supreme People's Court shall improve and perfect the normative system of judicial openness, focus on key areas and key links of the work of the people's courts and important judicial information of public concern, summarize the work experience of courts across the country, strengthen the standardization and normalization construction of judicial openness, actively study and introduce relevant technical standards and operating procedures, strengthen supervision and classified guidance, and continuously improve the quality and efficiency of judicial openness. Each High People's Court shall guide and promote the construction of standardization and normalization of judicial openness within its jurisdiction.

3. Improve and Standardize the Procedures for Judicial Openness

13. Improve the forms of judicial openness. The forms of judicial openness shall be adapted to local conditions and specific matters, authoritative and standardized, focus on practical results, facilitate the public to obtain timely and accurate information, and resolutely prevent formalism. If the Supreme People's Court has unified requirements on the form of judicial openness, the disclosure shall be carried out in accordance with the relevant requirements. Encourage grassroots people's courts to explore effective and popular forms of judicial openness among the masses. According to the actual situation, disclosure may be made through the following carriers:

(1) Newspapers, radio, television, the Internet, and other public media;

(2) Open the observance or reporting of court hearings in accordance with the Rules of the People's Court Courtroom;

(3) Gazettes, announcements, normative documents, or other official publications of the people's courts;

(4) Government websites of the people's courts or other authoritative website platforms;

(5) Press conferences, hearings, argumentation meetings, etc.;

(6) New media such as official microblogs, WeChat public accounts, news clients of the people's courts;

(7) Litigation service platforms such as the litigation service hall, litigation service network, 12368 litigation service hotline, and mobile mini-court of the people's courts;

(8) Other methods convenient for timely and accurate acquisition.

14. Unblock channels for parties and lawyers to obtain judicial information. For information disclosed only to the parties or interested persons, it must be strictly disclosed in accordance with the relevant procedural laws and regulations, and shall not be released to the public. On the premise of ensuring information security, information technology means may be fully used to provide convenience for parties or interested persons to obtain judicial information. Vigorously strengthen the construction of the lawyer service platform, provide convenience for lawyers to perform their duties according to law, and better play the important role of lawyers in promoting judicial service for the people and impartial justice.

15. Clarify the subject responsible for judicial openness. According to the principle of territorial management, centralized management, and hierarchical responsibility, clarify the subject responsible for each content of judicial openness, responsible for handling judicial openness matters, managing the content of openness, and responsible for its legality, completeness, accuracy, timeliness, and security. Establish and improve the coordination mechanism for judicial openness. If the disclosure content involves multiple people's courts, multiple internal institutions of the people's courts, or other units, it shall be disclosed after coordination to ensure the accuracy and completeness of judicial openness information.

16. Improve the process and management mechanism of judicial openness. Establish and improve the working mechanism of judicial openness, improve the work process, clarify management responsibilities, and promote judicial openness work in a standardized and orderly manner. Each department proposing matters to be disclosed shall verify and check the specific disclosure content, and if approval is required, it shall be disclosed after going through the approval procedures. Establish and improve the risk assessment mechanism before the disclosure of major sensitive matters. Establish and improve the tracking and response mechanism for social hot spots, strengthen the interpretation of judicial openness policies, and effectively respond to social concerns and judicial needs of the masses. For situations where public opinion has vague understanding or erroneous views due to lack of understanding, proactively release authoritative information to clarify facts and dispel doubts. The managers, operators, and other relevant responsible subjects of the judicial openness platform carriers shall, according to their authority, perform the duties of editing and checking and daily monitoring and management of the matters to be disclosed on their platforms.

17. Strictly implement the confidentiality review mechanism for judicial openness. Establish and improve the confidentiality review mechanism for judicial openness. When undertaking judicial openness matters, a confidentiality review shall be carried out simultaneously, strengthen the protection of state secrets, trial secrets, trade secrets, citizens' privacy rights, and personal information security, and achieve an organic unity of openness according to law and confidentiality. For matters within the scope of judicial openness, the classification work shall be carried out strictly in accordance with the scope of state secrets of the people's court work or already classified matters, and the scope of classification shall not be arbitrarily expanded.

4. Strengthen the Construction and Management of Judicial Openness Platform Carriers

18. Strengthen the work of gazettes and white papers of the people's courts. Give full play to the role of the gazette as a standard text and authoritative carrier of various important judicial information, timely and accurately publish important legal documents, judicial interpretations, judicial documents, judicial statistics, typical cases, and other important judicial information. Actively promote the digitization of historical gazettes, establish and improve a comprehensive database of people's court gazettes, and provide open online services. Focus on important judicial policies, major judicial measures, and important trial work conditions serving the overall situation, judicial service for the people, and impartial justice, and do a solid job in the preparation, production, publication, and promotion of white papers, and effectively enhance the authority, standardization, and readability of white papers. For white papers with important influence, strengthen promotion and recommendation, promote multilingual translation, and improve the dissemination and influence of the people's court white papers.

19. Strengthen the construction and management of government websites of the people's courts. Actively adapt to the trends of information technology development and changes in communication methods, improve the ability of people's court government websites to serve judicial openness, respond to social concerns, and promote the spirit of the rule of law, and strive to build people's court government websites into timely, accurate, standardized, and efficient judicial openness platforms, interactive communication platforms, and public service platforms. Strengthen the content construction and standardized management of government websites, strengthen information release and updates, promptly merge or close column sections without guaranteed content updates, and avoid affecting the effect of judicial openness due to untimely content updates, inaccurate information release, or no response to opinions and suggestions.

20. Strengthen the overall planning of the construction of government websites of courts nationwide. Prepare and improve the development guidelines for government websites of courts nationwide, clarify the functional positioning and content construction requirements of government websites of courts at four levels, and uniformly relevant technical standards at different levels. Promote the intensive construction of government websites of courts nationwide, and relocate the websites of grassroots people's courts that truly lack reliable human, financial, and mechanism guarantees to the technical platform of higher people's court websites for unified operation or to secure and controllable cloud service platforms to avoid duplicate construction and ensure technical security. Strengthen the coordination and linkage between government websites of people's courts at all levels, promote the construction of a network of government websites of courts nationwide, promote resource integration and sharing, form an integrated judicial openness service network, and enhance the communication effect of people's court government websites.

21. Further deepen the construction of the four major platforms for judicial openness. Deepen the construction of the China Trial Process Information Open Network, fully implement the provisions on disclosing trial process information through the Internet, improve relevant business regulations and technical standards, promote the automatic collection of online case handling data, and promote the precise push of trial process information. Expand the scope of court hearing openness, promote the live broadcast of court hearings on the Internet, and through the live broadcast of more cases, especially those with typical significance, actively accept social supervision, promote the improvement of judicial capacity, and deeply carry out rule of law education. Increase the comprehensive openness of judgments, strictly implement the mechanism for approving non-publication on the Internet, eliminate the problem of selective publication, standardize the management of judgments published on the Internet, and strengthen the research and utilization of judgment data resources. Increase the openness of enforcement information, expand the scope of enforcement information openness, promote the improvement of the credit punishment pattern of "one dishonesty,处处 restricted," strengthen open, transparent, and standardized enforcement, and promote high-level operation of enforcement work. Increase the integration of the construction of the four major platforms for judicial openness, pay attention to user experience, optimize platform functions, improve procedures and systems, pay more attention to the new characteristics of the mobile Internet era, and promote the transformation of the platform from one-way disclosure to multi-directional interaction, making litigation activities more transparent and litigation results more predictable.

22. Fully leverage modern information technology to promote judicial transparency. Make every effort to advance smart courts from initial formation to comprehensive construction, gradually achieving full online processing of all business, transparent procedures in accordance with law across the entire process, and comprehensive smart services. Explore the deep application of modern information technologies such as big data, cloud computing, artificial intelligence, and blockchain in judicial transparency, to promote the functions of automatic generation, intelligent analysis, full traceability, and permanent auditability of judicial information, thereby further enhancing the level of automation, informatization, and intelligence in judicial transparency. Deeply carry out research, mining, and expanded application of judicial big data, promote the nationwide comprehensive realization of synchronous generation and deep application of electronic case files along with case processing, strengthen the construction of the China Judicial Big Data Research Institute, and deepen the transformation and utilization of judicial big data research results. Vigorously strengthen cybersecurity construction, and effectively safeguard the information and data security of the people's courts.

23. Enhance the functional role of judicial transparency platforms in serving ethnic minority regions and in external publicity. Strengthen the construction of ethnic language sections on the government websites of the Supreme People's Court and people's courts in ethnic minority regions, as well as other important judicial transparency platforms, actively promote the translation of important judicial transparency content into ethnic languages, effectively safeguard the rights of people in ethnic minority regions to participate in and supervise judicial activities, and better meet the judicial needs of people in ethnic minority regions. Strengthen the construction of foreign language versions of judicial transparency platforms such as the Supreme People's Court government website and the International Commercial Court website, and reinforce the function of external publicity services. Maritime courts and courts with frequent foreign exchanges and a high number of foreign-related cases shall, based on their own conditions, promote the construction of foreign language versions or sections of judicial transparency platforms, and carry out multilingual translation and external publicity and promotion efforts.

24. Strengthen positive interaction with news media. Further smooth the channels of cooperation with news media, fully utilize news media resources, and proactively accept supervision by public opinion. Strengthen the news release work of the people's courts, establish and improve the spokesperson system for the people's courts, and improve the mechanism for cultivating and selecting outstanding spokespersons. Gradually establish a routine news release system covering courts nationwide, refine and standardize news release procedures and standards, and promptly and authoritatively release important judicial information such as major measures in the work of the people's courts and hot cases of social concern.

25. Strengthen the construction of the people's courts' own media and news publicity work. Strengthen the construction and management of the people's courts' own traditional media and new media platforms, promote the integrated development of traditional media and new media, fully utilize various new media platforms, broaden the channels of judicial transparency, and enhance the effectiveness of judicial transparency. Strengthen the news, public opinion, and publicity work of the people's courts in the new era, consciously undertake the mission of holding high the banner, gathering public support, cultivating new generations, promoting culture, and presenting a good image, firmly grasp the correct orientation of public opinion, fully demonstrate the major achievements in the construction of a rule-of-law China and the development of the judicial undertaking, and widely spread positive social energy.

V. Strengthening Organizational Guarantees

26. Implement the responsibility system for judicial transparency work. People's courts at all levels shall place judicial transparency work on their important议事日程, establish and improve the responsibility system for judicial transparency work, strengthen organizational leadership, coordinate and promote efforts, and further enhance the level of guarantee for judicial transparency. The president of each people's court bears the leadership responsibility for judicial transparency in that court, and shall listen to reports on judicial transparency work at least once a year, study and deploy, and supervise the implementation of key tasks to deepen judicial transparency. Refine and concretize the work responsibilities of each responsible department, strictly implement specific responsibilities in accordance with the scope of duties and authority, and promote the continuous deepening of judicial transparency work.

27. Improve the evaluation, supervision, and demonstration mechanisms. Refine the evaluation mechanism for the effectiveness of judicial transparency work, incorporate it into the performance appraisal system of the people's courts, and strengthen the assessment of aspects such as the accuracy, timeliness, and comprehensiveness of judicial transparency, platform construction, implementation of systems, and public satisfaction. Improve the supervision system for judicial transparency work, increase the intensity of supervision and guidance by higher courts over lower courts, supervise the implementation of the responsibility system for judicial transparency work, and ensure that various policies and measures for deepening judicial transparency are implemented and produce results. Give full play to the exemplary and leading role of model courts in judicial transparency, gradually expand the scope of model courts, summarize and promote the advanced experience of model courts, and lead the judicial transparency work of courts nationwide to continuously advance to a broader scope, higher level, and deeper degree.

28. Strengthen professional training on judicial transparency. Adhere to a demand-oriented approach, carry out training and exchanges on judicial transparency, and strengthen the study of judicial transparency policies and theories as well as the exercise of professional abilities. Incorporate judicial transparency business training into the training plans and regular training courses of the National Judges College and its branches. Leading cadres of the people's courts shall accurately grasp the new requirements and new deployments for judicial transparency, effectively enhance their perspective, timely update their concepts, strengthen their ability to use judicial transparency to drive court work, and improve their ability to interpret judicial policies and respond to social concerns in the context of the information age.

29. Strengthen investigation and research on judicial transparency. Solidly carry out practical research and theoretical research on judicial transparency, and accurately grasp the new requirements and new expectations of the people for deepening judicial transparency work. Pay attention to summarizing good experiences and good practices in judicial transparency practice, refine regular understandings, and promote the formation of high-quality theoretical research results and institutional transformation results. Adhere to a problem-oriented approach, focus on solving the deep-seated problems that constrain the optimization and upgrading of judicial transparency, actively absorb and draw on foreign theoretical achievements and practical experiences in judicial transparency based on China's judicial reality, and deeply promote theoretical, institutional, and practical innovation in judicial transparency.

30. Improve the judicial transparency supervision system. Broaden the channels for judicial transparency supervision, smooth the mechanisms for expressing and communicating public opinion, and consciously accept supervision by the People's Congress, democratic supervision, procuratorial supervision over litigation, and supervision by all sectors of society. Give full play to the supervision and interactive functions of judicial transparency platforms, establish and improve mechanisms for collecting, analyzing, transforming, and providing feedback on opinions, suggestions, complaints, and reports, earnestly absorb opinions and suggestions raised by the people, promptly study and resolve major issues reflected, and voluntarily publicize the adoption of suggestions and the resolution of issues, so as to better strengthen and improve the work of the people's courts.

31. Strengthen publicity and education on the rule of law. Strengthen the publicity of judicial transparency work, guide litigants and the public to correctly understand judicial transparency, better grasp the ways and means to obtain judicial transparency information, and ensure that the policies, measures, and results of the people's courts in deepening judicial transparency are known to, tested by, and recognized by the public. Strictly implement the responsibility system for legal popularization that "whoever enforces the law shall popularize the law", and through various forms of judicial transparency work, further disseminate knowledge of the constitution and laws, enhance the concept of the rule of law among the entire population, vigorously promote the core socialist values, and advance the integrated construction of a rule-of-law country, rule-of-law government, and rule-of-law society.

People's courts at all levels shall fully recognize the great significance of further deepening judicial transparency work, effectively unify their thinking and actions with the decisions and deployments of the Party Central Committee, conscientiously implement the requirements of these opinions, further clarify the key tasks of judicial transparency in their respective jurisdictions and units, formulate implementation measures, refine specific steps, and firmly grasp the work implementation, so as to form a new pattern of comprehensively deepening judicial transparency and strive to achieve new development in the work of the people's courts in the new era.

